module macrocycleQC
module ringOpeningQC

manifest AminoAcid_Val
manifest AminoAcid_Met
manifest AminoAcid_Ile
manifest AminoAcid_Thr
manifest AminoAcid_Pro
manifest AziridineAldehyde
manifest tBuNC
manifest PhCOSH
manifest TFE

instructions:

// ============================================================
// Synchronized Synthesis of Peptide-Based Macrocycles by
// Digital Microfluidics.
// Jebrail, Ng, Rai, Hili, Yudin, Wheeler -
// Angew. Chem. Int. Ed. 2010, 49, 8625-8629.
// DOI: 10.1002/anie.201001604
//
// PLATFORM: Two-plate DMF device. 10 reagent reservoirs,
// 88 actuation electrodes. Droplet volume: 900 nL each.
// Actuation: electrical potentials applied to electrode array
// coated with a hydrophobic insulator (Teflon-based surface).
// Solvent: trifluoroethanol (TFE) or deionized water.
//
// CHEMISTRY: Peptide-based macrocycles (PMs) are synthesized
// from three components in a one-step Ugi-type reaction:
//   (1) Amino acid (AA) -- 0.1 M in deionized water, 90 nmol
//   (2) Aziridine aldehyde -- 0.05 M in TFE, 45 nmol
//   (3) tert-butyl isocyanide (tBuNC) -- 0.1 M in TFE, 90 nmol
// Reaction: mixed 20 s (circular actuation on 4 electrodes),
// incubated 1 h at RT in parafilm-sealed Petri dish.
// Isolation: top plate removed; TFE evaporated 15 min at RT.
// Five PMs synthesized in parallel (Val, Met, Ile, Thr, Pro).
//
// RING-OPENING: PM aziridines are ring-opened by thiobenzoic
// acid (PhCOSH, 0.1 M in TFE, 90 nmol) to yield macrocyclic
// peptide thioesters (ring-opened products, ROPs).
// Re-dissolution: 4 x TFE droplets (~3.5 uL total) per PM
// spot. PhCOSH merged, incubated 1 h at RT. Isolated by
// TFE evaporation. Total steps: 30 (6 per parallel reaction).
//
// NINE-MEMBERED MACROCYCLE: Pro-Leu dipeptide substrate
// (0.1 M in TFE, 90 nmol) reacted with aziridine aldehyde
// and tBuNC. Incubation: 3 h at RT with mixing every 30 min.
// Produces a [4.2.0] nine-membered ring -- a ring size
// conventionally difficult to access by cyclic peptide synthesis.
//
// VERIFICATION: MS (ESI) and NMR used off-chip. Products
// re-dissolved in 100 uL MeOH + 0.1% formic acid (MS) or
// 250 uL CD3OD (NMR). Reaction kinetics: ~70% Met depletion
// in 1 h by DMF vs ~90% macroscale.
//
// NOTE ON `mix` ABSTRACTION: All `mix` statements model
// DMF electrode-actuated droplet merging and mixing. Active
// mixing is achieved by periodic circular actuation on 4
// electrodes (20 s). Incubation steps are modelled as
// `heat ... at 25c` (room temperature) for the stated
// duration.
//
// NOTE ON PARALLEL SYNTHESIS: BioScript does not support
// explicit parallelism. The five PM syntheses and their
// downstream ring-opening steps are encoded sequentially
// but represent simultaneous on-chip operations. All five
// amino acid droplets, all five aziridine aldehyde droplets,
// and all five tBuNC droplets are dispensed and merged as
// concurrent tracks on the physical DMF device.
//
// NOTE ON SOLVENT EVAPORATION: Isolation by solvent evaporation
// (top plate removal + 15 min RT wait) is modelled as
// `heat ... at 25c for 15m` following the pattern used in
// the reference BioScript files for analogous physical steps.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main               -- entry: parallel PM synthesis
//                              (5 x AA + AzAld + tBuNC),
//                              isolation, ring-opening (5 x),
//                              nine-membered macrocycle synthesis
//   BB2  macrocyclePass     -- macrocycleSignal > 0: PM verified
//                              by MS/NMR QC; dispose
//   BB3  macrocycleFail     -- macrocycleSignal <= 0: QC fail; drain
//   BB4  macrocycleJoin     -- join: ring-opening QC gate
//   BB5  ringOpeningPass    -- ringOpeningSignal > 0: ROP verified;
//                              dispose all ROP droplets
//   BB6  ringOpeningFail    -- ringOpeningSignal <= 0: QC fail;
//                              drain all ROP droplets
//   BB7  finalCleanup       -- terminal: dispose QC signals,
//                              experiment ends
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 -- PEPTIDE MACROCYCLE (PM) SYNTHESIS
// Five parallel tracks: Val, Met, Ile, Thr, Pro amino acids.
// Each track: dispense AA (900 nL) + AzAld (900 nL) + tBuNC
// (900 nL), merge, mix 20 s, incubate 1 h at RT.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// --- Track 1: Val ---

// STEP 1a: Dispense amino acid Val (0.1 M, deionized water).
aaVal        = dispense 1 units of AminoAcid_Val

// STEP 1b: Dispense aziridine aldehyde (0.05 M in TFE).
azAldVal     = dispense 1 units of AziridineAldehyde

// STEP 1c: Merge AA + aziridine aldehyde; mix 20 s (circular
//          actuation, 4 electrodes) to initiate imine formation.
aaMixVal     = mix aaVal with azAldVal for 20s

// STEP 1d: Dispense tBuNC (0.1 M in TFE).
tbuncVal     = dispense 1 units of tBuNC

// STEP 1e: Merge tBuNC into AA+AzAld droplet; mix 20 s.
//          This completes the three-component Ugi-type mix.
rxnMixVal    = mix aaMixVal with tbuncVal for 20s

// STEP 1f: Incubate 1 h at RT (parafilm-sealed Petri dish).
//          Macrocyclization proceeds to completion (~70% yield
//          on DMF vs ~90% macroscale within 1 h).
heat rxnMixVal at 25c for 60m

// STEP 1g: Isolate PM-Val by evaporating TFE (15 min, RT).
//          Top plate removed; solid PM precipitates on electrode.
heat rxnMixVal at 25c for 15m

// --- Track 2: Met ---

aaMet        = dispense 1 units of AminoAcid_Met
azAldMet     = dispense 1 units of AziridineAldehyde
aaMixMet     = mix aaMet with azAldMet for 20s
tbuncMet     = dispense 1 units of tBuNC
rxnMixMet    = mix aaMixMet with tbuncMet for 20s
heat rxnMixMet at 25c for 60m
heat rxnMixMet at 25c for 15m

// --- Track 3: Ile ---

aaIle        = dispense 1 units of AminoAcid_Ile
azAldIle     = dispense 1 units of AziridineAldehyde
aaMixIle     = mix aaIle with azAldIle for 20s
tbuncIle     = dispense 1 units of tBuNC
rxnMixIle    = mix aaMixIle with tbuncIle for 20s
heat rxnMixIle at 25c for 60m
heat rxnMixIle at 25c for 15m

// --- Track 4: Thr ---

aaThr        = dispense 1 units of AminoAcid_Thr
azAldThr     = dispense 1 units of AziridineAldehyde
aaMixThr     = mix aaThr with azAldThr for 20s
tbuncThr     = dispense 1 units of tBuNC
rxnMixThr    = mix aaMixThr with tbuncThr for 20s
heat rxnMixThr at 25c for 60m
heat rxnMixThr at 25c for 15m

// --- Track 5: Pro ---

aaPro        = dispense 1 units of AminoAcid_Pro
azAldPro     = dispense 1 units of AziridineAldehyde
aaMixPro     = mix aaPro with azAldPro for 20s
tbuncPro     = dispense 1 units of tBuNC
rxnMixPro    = mix aaMixPro with tbuncPro for 20s
heat rxnMixPro at 25c for 60m
heat rxnMixPro at 25c for 15m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 QC: MS/NMR off-chip verification of PM products.
// Representative QC performed on PM-Met (Fig. 4b, paper):
//   m/z 342 (PM-Met), confirmed against macroscale reference.
// macrocycleQC module abstracts ESI-MS + 1H-NMR readout.
// QC gate keyed on PM-Met as the representative track.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

macrocycleSignal = detect macrocycleQC on rxnMixMet for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: PM synthesis QC gate
// Pass (BB2): macrocycleSignal > 0 -> PM identity confirmed
//             by MS (m/z match) and NMR (chemical shifts);
//             dispose representative QC droplet.
// Fail (BB3): macrocycleSignal <= 0 -> MS/NMR mismatch;
//             drain representative droplet (synthesis failed).
// Both branches converge at BB4 (macrocycleJoin).
// ============================================================

if (macrocycleSignal > 0) {
    dispose rxnMixMet
} else {
    drain rxnMixMet
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: macrocycleJoin
// Dispose macrocycle QC signal droplet. Control falls into
// the aziridine ring-opening branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose macrocycleSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2 -- AZIRIDINE RING-OPENING (ROP) WITH PhCOSH
// Each dried PM spot is re-dissolved in 4 x TFE droplets
// (~3.5 uL total) driven to the dried residue by electrode
// actuation. PhCOSH (0.1 M in TFE, 900 nL) is dispensed,
// merged, mixed 20 s, and incubated 1 h at RT. Products
// are isolated by TFE evaporation (15 min, RT).
//
// NOTE ON RE-DISSOLUTION: Four TFE dispensing events are
// chained via sequential `mix` steps to accumulate ~3.5 uL
// (4 x 900 nL) on each dried PM spot, matching the paper's
// M&M. The compiler does not support multi-unit scalar
// dispense into a solid spot, so each TFE aliquot is
// dispensed individually and merged in sequence.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// --- ROP Track 1: Val ---

// Re-dissolve PM-Val with 4 x TFE aliquots (total ~3.5 uL).
tfe1Val      = dispense 1 units of TFE
tfe2Val      = dispense 1 units of TFE
tfe3Val      = dispense 1 units of TFE
tfe4Val      = dispense 1 units of TFE

tfeMix12Val  = mix tfe1Val with tfe2Val for 5s
tfeMix123Val = mix tfeMix12Val with tfe3Val for 5s
pmSolnVal    = mix tfeMix123Val with tfe4Val for 5s

// Merge re-dissolved PM-Val with PhCOSH; mix 20 s; incubate 1 h.
phcoshVal    = dispense 1 units of PhCOSH
ropMixVal    = mix pmSolnVal with phcoshVal for 20s
heat ropMixVal at 25c for 60m

// Isolate ROP-Val by TFE evaporation (15 min, RT).
heat ropMixVal at 25c for 15m

// --- ROP Track 2: Met ---

tfe1Met      = dispense 1 units of TFE
tfe2Met      = dispense 1 units of TFE
tfe3Met      = dispense 1 units of TFE
tfe4Met      = dispense 1 units of TFE

tfeMix12Met  = mix tfe1Met with tfe2Met for 5s
tfeMix123Met = mix tfeMix12Met with tfe3Met for 5s
pmSolnMet    = mix tfeMix123Met with tfe4Met for 5s

phcoshMet    = dispense 1 units of PhCOSH
ropMixMet    = mix pmSolnMet with phcoshMet for 20s
heat ropMixMet at 25c for 60m
heat ropMixMet at 25c for 15m

// --- ROP Track 3: Ile ---

tfe1Ile      = dispense 1 units of TFE
tfe2Ile      = dispense 1 units of TFE
tfe3Ile      = dispense 1 units of TFE
tfe4Ile      = dispense 1 units of TFE

tfeMix12Ile  = mix tfe1Ile with tfe2Ile for 5s
tfeMix123Ile = mix tfeMix12Ile with tfe3Ile for 5s
pmSolnIle    = mix tfeMix123Ile with tfe4Ile for 5s

phcoshIle    = dispense 1 units of PhCOSH
ropMixIle    = mix pmSolnIle with phcoshIle for 20s
heat ropMixIle at 25c for 60m
heat ropMixIle at 25c for 15m

// --- ROP Track 4: Thr ---

tfe1Thr      = dispense 1 units of TFE
tfe2Thr      = dispense 1 units of TFE
tfe3Thr      = dispense 1 units of TFE
tfe4Thr      = dispense 1 units of TFE

tfeMix12Thr  = mix tfe1Thr with tfe2Thr for 5s
tfeMix123Thr = mix tfeMix12Thr with tfe3Thr for 5s
pmSolnThr    = mix tfeMix123Thr with tfe4Thr for 5s

phcoshThr    = dispense 1 units of PhCOSH
ropMixThr    = mix pmSolnThr with phcoshThr for 20s
heat ropMixThr at 25c for 60m
heat ropMixThr at 25c for 15m

// --- ROP Track 5: Pro ---

tfe1Pro      = dispense 1 units of TFE
tfe2Pro      = dispense 1 units of TFE
tfe3Pro      = dispense 1 units of TFE
tfe4Pro      = dispense 1 units of TFE

tfeMix12Pro  = mix tfe1Pro with tfe2Pro for 5s
tfeMix123Pro = mix tfeMix12Pro with tfe3Pro for 5s
pmSolnPro    = mix tfeMix123Pro with tfe4Pro for 5s

phcoshPro    = dispense 1 units of PhCOSH
ropMixPro    = mix pmSolnPro with phcoshPro for 20s
heat ropMixPro at 25c for 60m
heat ropMixPro at 25c for 15m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2 QC: MS/NMR off-chip verification of ROP products.
// Representative QC on ROP-Met (Fig. 4c, paper): m/z 480.
// ringOpeningQC module abstracts ESI-MS + 1H-NMR readout.
// QC gate keyed on ROP-Met as the representative track.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ringOpeningSignal = detect ringOpeningQC on ropMixMet for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Ring-opening QC gate
// Pass (BB5): ringOpeningSignal > 0 -> ROP identity confirmed
//             (m/z 480 for ROP-Met); dispose all ROP droplets.
// Fail (BB6): ringOpeningSignal <= 0 -> MS/NMR mismatch;
//             drain all ROP droplets (ring-opening failed).
// Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (ringOpeningSignal > 0) {
    dispose ropMixVal
    dispose ropMixMet
    dispose ropMixIle
    dispose ropMixThr
    dispose ropMixPro
} else {
    drain ropMixVal
    drain ropMixMet
    drain ropMixIle
    drain ropMixThr
    drain ropMixPro
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose ring-opening QC signal.
//
// NOTE: The nine-membered macrocycle synthesis (Pro-Leu
// dipeptide substrate, Fig. 5, paper) represents an
// orthogonal demonstration on the same device type and is
// encoded below as a self-contained sub-protocol appended
// after the main QC gate. It does not branch into the
// existing CFG; it runs unconditionally after finalCleanup
// to reflect its status as a separate demonstration
// experiment in the paper (not a downstream product of
// the five-PM parallel synthesis above).
// ============================================================

dispose ringOpeningSignal

// ============================================================
// SUPPLEMENTARY PROTOCOL: Nine-Membered Macrocycle Synthesis
// (Pro-Leu dipeptide + AziridineAldehyde + tBuNC)
// Fig. 5a-b, paper. Produces compound 8 ([4.2.0] ring).
//
// Substrate: Pro-Leu dipeptide (0.1 M in TFE, 90 nmol, 900 nL).
// NOTE ON DIPEPTIDE MANIFEST: Pro-Leu dipeptide is modelled
// as AminoAcid_Pro here as BioScript requires all reagents to
// be declared in the manifest block at file header. In a
// full implementation, a separate manifest ProLeu_Dipeptide
// would be declared. The comment documents the physical
// reagent identity for compiler/user traceability.
//
// Reaction conditions differ from the five-PM protocol:
//   - Incubation: 3 h at RT (vs 1 h for single-AA PMs)
//   - Mixing: every 30 min (6 x 20s mixing events over 3 h)
//     modelled as alternating heat + mix steps.
//   - Ring size: 9-membered (vs 7-membered [4.1.0] for AA PMs)
//   - ESI-MS product peak: m/z 421 (Fig. 5b, paper)
// ============================================================

// STEP 9a: Dispense Pro-Leu dipeptide (modelled as AminoAcid_Pro;
//          see note above). 0.1 M in TFE, 900 nL, 90 nmol.
proLeu       = dispense 1 units of AminoAcid_Pro

// STEP 9b: Dispense aziridine aldehyde (0.05 M in TFE, 900 nL).
azAld9mer    = dispense 1 units of AziridineAldehyde

// STEP 9c: Merge dipeptide + aziridine aldehyde; mix 20 s.
dipepMix     = mix proLeu with azAld9mer for 20s

// STEP 9d: Dispense tBuNC (0.1 M in TFE, 900 nL).
tbunc9mer    = dispense 1 units of tBuNC

// STEP 9e: Merge tBuNC; mix 20 s to complete three-component mix.
rxnMix9mer   = mix dipepMix with tbunc9mer for 20s

// STEP 9f: Incubate 3 h at RT with periodic electrode mixing
//   every 30 min (paper M&M). BioScript has no in-place
//   agitation primitive and self-mix (var with same var) is
//   rejected by the symbol visitor as a double-consume.
//   The 3 h incubation is therefore encoded as a single
//   heat statement (180 min). The periodic 20 s electrode
//   actuations are a physical device operation implicit in
//   the DMF controller firmware and do not consume or
//   produce a new droplet variable.
heat rxnMix9mer at 25c for 180m

// STEP 9g: Isolate nine-membered macrocycle by TFE evaporation
//          (15 min at RT). Top plate removed; solid product
//          precipitates. ESI-MS: m/z 421 (compound 8, Fig. 5b).
heat rxnMix9mer at 25c for 15m

// Final disposal of nine-membered macrocycle product droplet.
dispose rxnMix9mer

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
